  <h2>Start Here</h2>
  <p>
    Gen Coupe Swaps is a free, step-by-step resource for putting a GM LS V8 into a Hyundai Genesis Coupe, both the BK1 (2009–2012) and the BK2 (2013–2016).
    It started as one builder's wiring notes in a Google Doc and grew into a full set of guides covering every system you'll touch:
    engine and mounts, wiring and the Holley ECU, cooling, fuel, transmission, driveshaft, rear end, brakes, and the small stuff like A/C, gas pedals, and reverse lights.
  </p>
  <p>
    Everything here comes from real swaps, with photos, wire colors, pin numbers, and part numbers, plus vendor specs and sources linked on each page.
    Wire colors and pinouts change between years and between 2.0T and 3.8 cars, so always confirm against your own car and the
    <a href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1p-_n4A5JZTp92iz3rK1sQcm1jPLSvz5W?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">factory shop manuals</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>BK1 vs BK2: What Changes for the Swap</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th>BK1 (2009–2012)</th><th>BK2 (2013–2016)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Front clearance</td><td>Tighter: use a Corvette-spacing accessory drive</td><td>About 1.5" more room between engine and fans</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Factory engine mount</td><td>Three studs to the subframe</td><td>Single center stud (LOJ mounts are designed around this one)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mount kits</td><td>LOJ mounts need the subframe drilled (tools included). Check your kit.</td><td>Bolts in</td></tr>
      <tr><td>In-tank fuel pump</td><td>DeatschWerks DW420 (2010–12)</td><td>DeatschWerks DW430C (2013–16 3.8)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>OEM gas pedal pinout</td><td>BK1 pinout</td><td>Different BK2 pinout</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Details are in <a href="/guides/swap-kits#motor-mounts">Motor Mounts</a>, <a href="/guides/engine-selection#spacing">accessory drive spacing</a>, <a href="/guides/fuel-system#pump">fuel pumps</a>, and <a href="/guides/gas-pedal#oem">gas pedal pinouts</a>.</p>

  <h2>The Swap, Step by Step</h2>
  <p>A typical order of attack. Each step links to its full guide.</p>
  <ol class="roadmap">
    <li><a href="/guides/engine-selection"><strong>Pick the engine</strong></a>: 5.3, 6.0, LS1, LS3 or supercharged, plus accessory spacing and 24x vs 58x crank reluctor.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/swap-kits"><strong>Choose a swap kit</strong></a> and <a href="/guides/swap-kits#motor-mounts">motor mounts</a>: Sikky, LOJ, ISR or CX Racing, with a Genesis-specific oil pan.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/transmission"><strong>Transmission &amp; clutch</strong></a>: T56 Magnum XL specs, pilot bushing, shifter, and the Wilwood clutch master fix.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/driveshaft"><strong>Driveshaft</strong></a> and <a href="/guides/differential">rear end</a>: the 3-to-4 bolt adapter, sedan axles, and the Ford 8.8 IRS for big power.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/wiring"><strong>Wiring</strong></a>: passenger fuse box, push to start, ECU cranking power, reverse lights.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/ecu"><strong>ECU &amp; tuning</strong></a>: choosing a Holley Terminator X kit, dash mounting, speedo.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/fuel-system"><strong>Fuel system</strong></a>: in-tank pump, dedicated relay, EVAP.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/cooling"><strong>Cooling</strong></a>: radiator, fans and relays, steam vent line, heater hoses.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/alternator"><strong>Alternator</strong></a>, <a href="/guides/power-steering">power steering</a>, <a href="/guides/ac">A/C</a>, and <a href="/guides/gas-pedal">gas pedal</a>.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/intake"><strong>Intake</strong></a> and <a href="/guides/exhaust">exhaust &amp; heat shielding</a>: hood clearance, headers, and keeping heat off the fuse box.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/brakes"><strong>Brakes</strong></a>: ABS delete, proportioning valve, line lock.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/troubleshooting"><strong>Troubleshooting</strong></a>: quick fixes for overheating, charging, fans, no-start and more.</li>
  </ol>

