  <h2>Before You Begin</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Join the Facebook groups <a href="https://www.facebook.com/share/g/19PJahbKRm/?mibextid=wwXIfr" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Swapped GCs</a> and <a href="https://www.facebook.com/share/g/1KYpk5EjgQ/?mibextid=wwXIfr" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Genesis Coupe LS Swaps</a>. That's where most wiring photos and real build logs get shared.</li>
    <li>On a BK1, use Corvette accessory spacing for radiator clearance.</li>
    <li>Plan a serious radiator and fan setup, the steam vent line, and an oil cooler from the start. Heat is the number-one LS Gen Coupe headache.</li>
    <li>Buy mounts, oil pan, and headers from the same kit maker so everything lines up.</li>
  </ul>

